# PLAINTEXT SHAPE of secret.sops.yaml - this example is NOT read by kustomize and holds no secret.
#
# The Gitea PAT the watchdog uses, held by `org-ops-bot`: a NON-admin member of the org's Owners
# team. It is never the site-admin `chifor`, whose token could force-merge past branch protection.
# Scopes, while the watchdog ships in shadow mode (DRY_RUN=true):
#   read:organization  GET /orgs/cchifor/actions/runners (org-owner only) and /orgs/cchifor/repos
#   read:repository    GET runs, jobs, open pulls and branches per repo
# read:admin is NOT needed on Gitea 1.26 (verified 2026-10-06). Before DRY_RUN=false the rerun
# POST (/repos/{o}/{r}/actions/runs/{id}/rerun-failed-jobs) needs Actions write. Gitea has no
# Actions-specific token scope (those endpoints sit under write:repository), so give it a SECOND
# token, scope write:repository, from a NON-owner bot whose team grants only the Actions unit at
# write (repo.actions) - never write:repository on this owner bot.
# Mint it ONCE, in the gitea pod (PAT scopes are immutable; a wrong set means a new token):
#   kubectl --context admin@ai -n gitea exec deploy/gitea -c gitea -- \
#     gitea admin user generate-access-token --raw -u org-ops-bot -t org-ops-watchdog-<date> \
#       --scopes read:organization,read:repository
# then, on the workstation with the age key (kubernetes/infra/_out/age.agekey, main checkout):
#   cp secret.sops.yaml.example secret.sops.yaml          # in kubernetes/apps/apps/ci-rerun-watchdog/
#   (paste the token over REPLACE_ME in an editor - never via a shell command that lands in history)
#   sops --encrypt --in-place secret.sops.yaml            # .sops.yaml's generic rule: data|stringData
#   verify `- secret.sops.yaml` is listed in kustomization.yaml and commit ONLY the encrypted file.
# `git diff` must show ENC[...] for `token` and nothing else in plaintext.
apiVersion: v1
kind: Secret
metadata:
  name: ci-rerun-watchdog-gitea
  namespace: ci-rerun-watchdog
type: Opaque
stringData:
  token: REPLACE_ME
